<ContentLayout title="Free Website Audit Report: Download Editable HTML Findings" description="Generate a free report from pasted page HTML and download the findings as Markdown. Add evidence and assigned actions using the agency toolkit." breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} publishDate="2026-03-28" updateDate="2026-09-05" showCTA={false}>
<h2>What the Free Report Contains</h2><p>The checker report contains a timestamp, a scope statement and the actual HTML observations. Each check includes a status, evidence and a suggested next step. It does not include a crawl score, backlink analysis, speed measurements or a promise of revenue gains.</p>
<p><a href="/free-website-audit/">Open the free HTML SEO checker</a> to inspect your page source.</p>
<h2>Download and Edit Your Findings</h2><p>Run the HTML checker and choose Download findings. Open the .md file in a text editor or Markdown editor. Add affected URLs and your interpretation. Review potentially sensitive page text before sending the report to someone else.</p>
<h2>Turn Findings into an Action Plan</h2><p>Confirm whether each observation is an issue for the page. A noindex directive can be intentional and an empty alt attribute can be correct for decorative images. Assign confirmed fixes to an owner and define the evidence needed to close each task.</p>
<p>Use the <a href="/resources/agency-audit-toolkit/">editable agency toolkit</a> to record evidence and implementation steps. The <a href="/website-audit-checklist/template/">50-check PDF</a> covers a wider manual review.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/case-studies/auditweb-self-audit/">documented self-audit</a> provides real examples of observations and corrections. Review the <a href="/website-audit-services/">professional audit scope</a> if the problem requires evidence beyond your page source.</p>
</ContentLayout>
